From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:59:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.web: the rest of Windows.Web.Http, measured against
 Windows.

React Native in Office (AugLoop, Backstage) sends its requests through
HttpClient and reads them back through the header collections and
content streams, and what was here stopped short of both.  This is the
namespace whole, each part matched line by line against probes run on
Windows:

- The header value classes, seventeen of them, with Parse and
  TryParse, and the thirteen header collections, parsed and written the
  way Windows writes them ("gzip,deflate;q=0.5" reads back as "gzip,
  deflate; q=0.5").
- The request, response and content header collections: Insert, Append
  and TryAppendWithoutValidation with Windows' validation; typed
  properties that hand out the object a header is kept as, the same one
  every time, written from whenever it is read; Location, Referer and
  Content-Location kept as a Uri and read as its AbsoluteCanonicalUri,
  Host as a HostName read as its canonical name.  The headers are
  listed as ATL's CAtlMap keeps them, 17 bins by the FNV-1a hash of the
  name in upper case, rehashed past 38, which is the order Windows lists
  and sends them in.
- HttpStringContent, HttpBufferContent, HttpStreamContent,
  HttpFormUrlEncodedContent, HttpMultipartContent and
  HttpMultipartFormDataContent, loaded on demand; a body read as text
  the way Windows reads it: its charset, else its byte order mark, else
  UTF-8 for JSON and ISO-8859-1 for anything else, and E_FAIL for a
  charset Windows does not know.  The buffers a content hands out are
  exactly as long as what they hold, of a class named
  Windows.Storage.Streams.IBuffer.
- HttpClient with IHttpClient2 and 3 and the Try* methods,
  HttpRequestMessage and HttpResponseMessage, HttpMethod, the async
  operations with their progress.
- HttpBaseProtocolFilter over WinINet, with interfaces 2 to 5:
  redirects followed here, as Windows follows them, so that a POST
  redirected to a GET still carries the Cache-Control WinINet gave it;
  decompression, cache control, credentials, ignorable certificate
  errors, cookies through HttpCookieManager.

Not yet: ServerCustomValidationRequested is kept but never raised, and
the transport information carries no server certificate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 937f6aabb6750047c1cc68b802ebfa8bab8f2366)

